  "body": "Extend `EdgeBreak` records and simulation credit so 3D bisector chamfers, concave ball breaks, vertical corner breaks, and rounded multi-pass breaks verify clean while keeping #529 safety bounds strict.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/cl/src/cl/edge_break.rs` (`EdgeBreak`)\n- `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/edge_break.rs` (`credit_breaks`)\n- `crates/app/src/stock_sim_breaks.rs` (`bounded`)\n- `crates/app/src/project/file.rs`\n\n## What to change\n\n1. Generalize `EdgeBreak` beyond vertical-axis cone slopes (`edge, depth, slope`) to describe 3D edge-break volumes: edge polyline with local outward bisector frames, break profile (flat bisector chamfer, concave ball arc of radius `R`, or convex rounded profile), and declared width and depth.\n2. Update `credit_breaks` (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/edge_break.rs`) to test removed material inside the 3D break volume, including steep, vertical, and oblique bisector edges where top-down XY distance fails.\n3. Preserve #529 upper-bound checks in `EdgeBreak::is_sane`, project loading, and `stock_sim_breaks::bounded`. Drop out-of-bound or corrupted records by name, and still convict gouges outside the declared break.\n4. Keep compatibility for existing 2D `Chamfer2D` and v1 cone `Deburr` `EdgeBreak` records.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Valid 3D bisector chamfers, concave ball breaks (`R >= w / 2`), and rounded edge breaks verify clean with zero false gouge verdicts.\n- Inflated or corrupted `EdgeBreak` records fail bounds checks and drop by name.\n- Real gouges outside the declared edge break still convict in stock verification, pinned by sim and app tests.\n\nPart of #1827\n",
